# I feel ill in Russian: у меня болит голова
subtitle: "Say where it hurts and how you feel in Russian: у меня́ боли́т голова́, мне пло́хо, and ask for a doctor or a pharmacy."
teaches: ["vocabulary/health"]
thumb: "band \"My head hurts: 'by me hurts head'\" note \"Мне пло́хо\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Whose is it in Russian: чей, чья, чьё","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/39-russian-whose.cast"}

## I feel ill in Russian: у меня болит голова
level: basic

    icon i_sore size 150 set twemoji x 500 y 560 or ["face with thermometer"] icon_look picture of "face with head-bandage" hidden true
    glossed g_head "У меня́ боли́т голова́." say_voice b gloss ["by","me","hurts","head"] show_gloss under x 500 y 360 font_size 72 hidden true
